. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * 
. 
.         * Please add a verbal description of your model here:
. 
.         /*
> We estimate the effect of having a daughter compared to having a son as a fir
> st child on political preferences. Yi,t represents our outcome variable, a va
> lue for political preferences between far right and far left, ranging from ze
> ro to ten. As before, variable d_daughter represents the indicator variable f
> or having a daughter as a first child and our coefficient of interest is esti
> mated by 1. The rest of the equation remains unchanged, Xi,t represents the
>  same set of control variables, and we include survey wave fixed effects, rep
> resented by t to "capture" any influence common to all parents in that spec
> ific wave —like macro shocks, policy changes, or trends—thereby controlling f
> or time-specific confounders.
> We take the family as the unit that is treated and hence based on Abadie et a
> l. (2022)cluster standard errors at the household level.
>         */
.         
.         reghdfe left d_daughter n_brothers n_sisters fchild_age, absorb (syea
> r) cluster(hid)
